    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Smallest square around it",
        "body": "The glued tiles reach across **4 columns** (from the left tile to the right tile) and 3 rows. A square that contains them must be at least 4 tiles wide, so at least $4 \\times 4 = 16$ tiles.\n\nA 4 × 4 square works: put the shape in it. She needs $16 - 6 = 10$ more tiles.\n\n**Answer: (D) 10**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Fill the gaps",
        "body": "Draw a 4 × 4 square around the shape. Count the empty places row by row: the top row has 3 empty, the second row 1, the third row 2, and the bottom row 4. $3 + 1 + 2 + 4 = 10$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 10**"
      }
    ],
