        "title": "Find a short path",
        "body": "From room A:\n\n1. Go right through the door into the long top room.\n2. Go down through the door on the right part of its floor into the room below.\n3. Go down again into the room under it (on the right of the middle wall).\n4. Go right through the door into room B.\n\nThat is 4 doors.\n\nCould 3 be enough? B has only two neighbouring rooms (the one on its left and the one above it), and neither of them can be reached from A through just 2 doors. So 4 is the least.\n\n**Answer: (B) 4**"
